1
00:00:04,738 --> 00:00:07,507
Where did Akira go?

2
00:00:10,443 --> 00:00:12,779
What's he doing?

3
00:00:30,563 --> 00:00:31,531
Forget it.

4
00:00:52,452 --> 00:00:53,453
<i>Hello?</i>

5
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:55,388
Akira?

6
00:00:56,256 --> 00:00:58,191
Why aren't you back?

7
00:00:58,258 --> 00:00:59,192
Where are you?

8
00:00:59,592 --> 00:01:00,527
<i>Michiko,</i>

9
00:01:00,994 --> 00:01:02,495
<i>you ran away from home.</i>

10
00:01:03,096 --> 00:01:06,833
MICHIKO DAIMON, FREELANCE SURGEON

11
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,701
I have nowhere to go.

12
00:01:09,269 --> 00:01:10,703
<i>How silly.</i>

13
00:01:13,139 --> 00:01:16,943
Hurry on home and make me dinner.

14
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:19,279
I'm starving.

15
00:01:19,946 --> 00:01:21,714
<i>You need to be independent.</i>

16
00:01:22,282 --> 00:01:24,684
<i>I'm busy expanding business.</i>

17
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:28,721
<i>I'm getting work</i>
<i>so I'll be gone for a while.</i>

18
00:01:28,788 --> 00:01:29,689
What?

19
00:01:30,123 --> 00:01:34,394
<i>Don't forget to feed Ben Casey.</i>
<i>That's all.</i>

20
00:01:34,461 --> 00:01:36,629
Wait. You can't come home?

21
00:01:36,696 --> 00:01:37,864
Akira!

22
00:01:42,235 --> 00:01:44,237
What's going on?

23
00:01:44,571 --> 00:01:47,874
<i>This is a story about</i>
<i>a maverick female doctor.</i>

24
00:01:49,576 --> 00:01:53,847
<i>In 2014, medical establishments</i>
<i>collapsed and became more corrupt.</i>

25
00:01:53,913 --> 00:01:55,014
JAPAN MEDICAL INDUSTRY ASSOCIATION

26
00:01:55,081 --> 00:01:57,117
<i>Medicine, which handles lives,</i>

27
00:01:57,717 --> 00:02:00,987
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

28
00:02:03,857 --> 00:02:05,758
Following a cabinet decision,

29
00:02:06,392 --> 00:02:10,964
I declare the establishment of
the Specified National Research

30
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:15,969
and Development Corporation,
the Japan Healthcare Organization.

31
00:02:20,106 --> 00:02:23,042
Let me introduce to you

32
00:02:23,109 --> 00:02:27,013
the first chairman. Mr. Yoshihito Tendo,

33
00:02:27,547 --> 00:02:28,414
please.

34
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:43,329
My dream has come true.

35
00:02:43,396 --> 00:02:48,034
Concentrating all resources
and funds related to healthcare,

36
00:02:48,101 --> 00:02:53,339
this is a healthcare organization
of the next generation.

37
00:02:53,973 --> 00:02:56,376
It will provide quality care worldwide.

38
00:02:58,478 --> 00:03:00,813
<i>However, despite these conditions,</i>

39
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:03,383
<i>Japan announced to export</i>

40
00:03:03,449 --> 00:03:07,787
<i>state of the art medical services</i>
<i>as a growth strategy.</i>

41
00:03:08,321 --> 00:03:12,492
<i>Healthcare entered an era</i>
<i>of the strong preying on the weak.</i>

42
00:03:12,559 --> 00:03:15,128
We are off on a new start...

43
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:16,863
He really made it.

44
00:03:17,297 --> 00:03:21,000
Mr. Tendo has obtained
the ultimate authority

45
00:03:21,067 --> 00:03:22,669
that a doctor can have.

46
00:03:22,735 --> 00:03:24,571
It's only right.

47
00:03:25,071 --> 00:03:28,074
It's all because
we saved diet member Tokachi

48
00:03:28,141 --> 00:03:30,476
using the Fujikawa Method.

49
00:03:34,781 --> 00:03:36,416
TODAY

50
00:03:37,817 --> 00:03:41,754
<i>Then came freelance doctors</i>
<i>who don't belong to hospitals.</i>

51
00:03:41,821 --> 00:03:42,655
AKIRA, WHEN ARE YOU COMING BACK?

52
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:45,858
<i>In other words, maverick doctors.</i>

53
00:03:46,292 --> 00:03:48,294
With this organization...

54
00:03:48,361 --> 00:03:50,797
Mr. Tendo's been promoted

55
00:03:50,863 --> 00:03:53,800
and the president's seat will be open.

56
00:03:53,866 --> 00:03:58,304
Meaning, the question is
who will be taking that seat.

57
00:03:59,205 --> 00:04:00,840
The East and West showdown.

58
00:04:01,274 --> 00:04:05,111
I have a much bigger advantage.

59
00:04:05,645 --> 00:04:09,983
God...Buddha...Sir Tendo...

60
00:04:10,717 --> 00:04:13,553
Please don't abandon me.

61
00:04:14,654 --> 00:04:16,623
Healthcare in Japan will change.

62
00:04:18,291 --> 00:04:19,225
Please...

63
00:04:20,326 --> 00:04:22,195
Change and challenge.

64
00:04:22,629 --> 00:04:24,631
The West is overly confident.

65
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:27,967
The East is praying.

66
00:04:29,836 --> 00:04:31,537
YOSHIHITO TENDO, CHAIRMAN

67
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:32,905
That is all.

68
00:04:35,241 --> 00:04:36,876
It seems Dr. Fujikawa

69
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:40,013
has proven victorious in the showdown.

70
00:04:43,216 --> 00:04:45,118
Quiet!

71
00:04:46,986 --> 00:04:47,920
Daimon.

72
00:04:48,488 --> 00:04:50,356
Say something.

73
00:04:50,757 --> 00:04:52,025
I won't do that.

74
00:04:52,759 --> 00:04:56,162
In reality, it was Dr. Daimon

75
00:04:56,229 --> 00:04:58,298
who operated on Ms. Tokachi.

76
00:04:58,364 --> 00:05:00,300
How dare you say that.

77
00:05:00,366 --> 00:05:03,002
What is your problem?

78
00:05:04,504 --> 00:05:07,073
He's not answering.

79
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:12,679
Demon, where'd you get these fans?

80
00:05:13,112 --> 00:05:14,113
- These?
- Yeah.

81
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:17,417
Her secretary gave them
celebrate her recovery.

82
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:22,322
YOSHIKO TOKACHI

83
00:05:27,293 --> 00:05:28,461
Isn't this bad?

84
00:05:32,498 --> 00:05:33,599
It's here.

85
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:36,202
Even while I'm gone,

86
00:05:36,602 --> 00:05:39,572
operate and make lots of money.

87
00:05:40,373 --> 00:05:41,641
Roger.

88
00:05:41,708 --> 00:05:43,810
I'm going to operate.

89
00:05:46,045 --> 00:05:47,980
If I become the president,

90
00:05:48,047 --> 00:05:49,916
I owe it to you.

91
00:05:53,219 --> 00:05:54,487
- Excuse me.
- Come in.

92
00:05:54,554 --> 00:05:56,089
MASUMI IKAWA, SECRETARY TO DR. TENDO

93
00:05:56,155 --> 00:05:57,423
Mr. Tendo asked me

94
00:05:57,957 --> 00:06:01,160
to have you sign and date this.

95
00:06:03,229 --> 00:06:04,297
Already?

96
00:06:08,067 --> 00:06:09,769
RESIGNATION

97
00:06:15,308 --> 00:06:17,477
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

98
00:06:17,944 --> 00:06:21,314
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

99
00:06:22,014 --> 00:06:26,652
<i>Her medical license</i>
<i>and experience are her only weapons.</i>

100
00:06:29,155 --> 00:06:30,223
Let's begin.

101
00:06:30,289 --> 00:06:31,457
Yes.

102
00:06:35,762 --> 00:06:36,696
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

103
00:06:55,515 --> 00:06:57,183
Michiko Daimon...

104
00:07:05,958 --> 00:07:08,461
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

105
00:07:09,562 --> 00:07:12,765
<i>also known as "Doctor-X."</i>

106
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:43,863
Mr. Tendo.

107
00:07:44,864 --> 00:07:48,868
Congratulations on becoming

108
00:07:49,368 --> 00:07:53,606
the Japan Healthcare
Organization chairman.

109
00:07:53,673 --> 00:07:55,208
Congratulations.

110
00:07:55,274 --> 00:07:57,343
- Thank you. Have a seat.
- Thank you.

111
00:07:57,777 --> 00:07:59,145
- Fujikawa, please.
- Yes.

112
00:08:02,248 --> 00:08:04,183
Some manju buns.

113
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:08,921
You people never learn.

114
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:13,326
We at Seikyo University

115
00:08:14,126 --> 00:08:19,632
helped a great deal
for Ms. Tokachi's surgery.

116
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,436
Myocardial regeneration...

117
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:26,572
Liver regeneration
with bone marrow cells...

118
00:08:27,039 --> 00:08:28,107
All of these,

119
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:31,577
every single one,

120
00:08:32,445 --> 00:08:36,482
are thanks to the research
by Seikyo University.

121
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:41,954
Also...there's one more thing.

122
00:08:42,288 --> 00:08:46,526
Mr. Tendo.

123
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:54,433
You'll become the chairman.
of the Japan Healthcare Organization.

124
00:08:55,067 --> 00:09:01,407
So this seat of the Care Center
will be open.

125
00:09:02,775 --> 00:09:06,946
Who will be sitting
in this seat after you?

126
00:09:07,013 --> 00:09:09,882
I can't help but wonder.

127
00:09:11,183 --> 00:09:12,785
Who will sit here?

128
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:20,593
President.

129
00:09:21,327 --> 00:09:27,199
What Fujikawa did

130
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:31,337
was just faithfully carry out your orders.

131
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:34,840
You insist on firing him,

132
00:09:34,907 --> 00:09:37,276
but he's quite troubled.

133
00:09:37,343 --> 00:09:38,411
Yes, sir.

134
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,382
I have one more...

135
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:46,385
Favor to ask.

136
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:50,823
There's a patient

137
00:09:51,757 --> 00:09:53,559
I must have treated here

138
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:56,896
at the Care Center.

139
00:09:57,396 --> 00:09:58,864
Who is it?

140
00:09:59,398 --> 00:10:00,299
Well...

141
00:10:05,304 --> 00:10:06,305
Me.

142
00:10:09,342 --> 00:10:11,444
Dr. Hiruma, are you ill?

143
00:10:11,877 --> 00:10:14,413
That is terrible.

144
00:10:16,082 --> 00:10:20,453
Is it something
not treatable at Seikyo University?

145
00:10:21,687 --> 00:10:22,622
It's not.

146
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:27,093
I want to get help

147
00:10:28,995 --> 00:10:35,534
from a doctor from the Care Center.

148
00:10:35,601 --> 00:10:36,769
Who?

149
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:41,107
Dr. Michiko Daimon.

150
00:10:42,708 --> 00:10:44,043
Oh.

151
00:10:44,110 --> 00:10:45,878
Unless it's her...

152
00:10:47,947 --> 00:10:51,584
I don't think my illness can be treated.

153
00:10:53,285 --> 00:10:54,320
Well then...

154
00:10:56,956 --> 00:11:00,259
I shall accept in exchange

155
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:01,894
Dr. Fujikawa's resignation.

156
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:03,162
What?

157
00:11:08,401 --> 00:11:10,336
I understand.

158
00:11:10,403 --> 00:11:12,171
- Alright, Fujikawa?
- Wait,

159
00:11:12,238 --> 00:11:13,639
you're breaking our promise.

160
00:11:13,706 --> 00:11:15,708
What promise?

161
00:11:15,775 --> 00:11:17,009
What?

162
00:11:17,076 --> 00:11:19,378
Mr. Tendo doesn't need you anymore.

163
00:11:19,445 --> 00:11:20,913
- Nothing I can do...
- But...

164
00:11:20,980 --> 00:11:21,847
No "buts."

165
00:11:21,914 --> 00:11:24,684
My life cannot be sacrificed.

166
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:25,985
Damn you!

167
00:11:26,652 --> 00:11:27,820
This is a joke.

168
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:30,923
I'm getting fired for a part-timer?

169
00:11:30,990 --> 00:11:32,458
Don't say part-timer.

170
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:34,060
With your skills,

171
00:11:34,126 --> 00:11:36,796
you can make it as a part-timer.

172
00:11:37,830 --> 00:11:38,964
Help me.

173
00:11:41,133 --> 00:11:42,334
So it's decided.

174
00:11:42,401 --> 00:11:43,669
Yes.

175
00:11:43,736 --> 00:11:46,138
Then I will see you at the conference.

176
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:47,139
Yes.

177
00:11:49,942 --> 00:11:51,477
Dr. Fujikawa.

178
00:11:52,778 --> 00:11:54,814
What a waste.

179
00:11:56,882 --> 00:11:57,983
You're right.

180
00:12:10,796 --> 00:12:12,164
Too obnoxious.

181
00:12:18,170 --> 00:12:22,441
Akira, answer me.

182
00:12:23,776 --> 00:12:25,211
Shut up.

183
00:12:25,811 --> 00:12:27,413
Please begin.

184
00:12:27,947 --> 00:12:29,849
As you all know,

185
00:12:31,150 --> 00:12:35,454
I will be leaving
this hospital in a few weeks.

186
00:12:35,521 --> 00:12:36,422
JUNKO SHIRAKI, HEAD NURSE

187
00:12:36,489 --> 00:12:40,559
I believe this will be
my final conference.

188
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:44,897
I ask that you all use your wisdom

189
00:12:46,332 --> 00:12:51,170
to save this patient here.

190
00:12:52,972 --> 00:12:56,375
As for Surgical Director Fujikawa,

191
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:58,744
he resigned yesterday.

192
00:13:01,213 --> 00:13:02,414
No way.

193
00:13:03,949 --> 00:13:06,919
I would like for
East and West to come together

194
00:13:07,653 --> 00:13:13,259
and work under Unified
Surgical Department Director Ebina.

195
00:13:13,859 --> 00:13:14,894
Yes!

196
00:13:16,695 --> 00:13:17,530
Yes, sir.

197
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:25,004
Please begin my final conference.

198
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:29,842
Today's first case.

199
00:13:29,909 --> 00:13:31,343
63-year-old male.

200
00:13:32,344 --> 00:13:35,748
He has transverse colon and rectal cancer,

201
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:39,752
synchronous
multiple colon cancer stage IV.

202
00:13:40,219 --> 00:13:42,521
Liver metastasis as well.

203
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:54,333
The patient will be participating in the
conference this time. Please come in.

204
00:14:02,007 --> 00:14:03,542
Director Hiruma?

205
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:07,546
The East and West battle hasn't ended.

206
00:14:09,882 --> 00:14:13,519
Thank you. Thanks.

207
00:14:15,287 --> 00:14:16,255
Thank you.

208
00:14:23,996 --> 00:14:27,299
Dr. Hiruma, a great senior of you all.

209
00:14:28,601 --> 00:14:33,405
He strongly requested to be present here,

210
00:14:33,472 --> 00:14:36,575
so we will continue like this.

211
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:41,113
Hello.

212
00:14:42,381 --> 00:14:43,449
It's been a while.

213
00:14:45,384 --> 00:14:46,752
- Ebina.
- Yes.

214
00:14:47,286 --> 00:14:49,288
Satoru Ebina.

215
00:14:49,355 --> 00:14:50,356
It's Takashi.

216
00:14:51,857 --> 00:14:52,691
Takashi.

217
00:14:56,662 --> 00:14:57,663
Achi!

218
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:58,797
Yes.

219
00:14:58,864 --> 00:15:00,299
Long time no see.

220
00:15:01,166 --> 00:15:02,301
Smile more.

221
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:07,439
The West looks so down.

222
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:11,844
But I too, as you can see...

223
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:15,114
I have ended up

224
00:15:15,948 --> 00:15:20,452
as some old man with a serious illness.

225
00:15:22,154 --> 00:15:25,925
I ask that you work together

226
00:15:27,293 --> 00:15:30,429
in order to save me.

227
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:33,198
Yes, sir.

228
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:35,267
Yes, sir.

229
00:15:35,734 --> 00:15:37,636
"Yes, sir" is so nice.

230
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,173
PATIENT: JUCHIRO HIRUMA

231
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:43,008
Juichiro Hiruma?

232
00:15:43,075 --> 00:15:45,244
Shigekatsu wasn't his real name.

233
00:15:45,644 --> 00:15:49,281
It's hard to say
in front of the patient...

234
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:53,452
But I believe removal will be difficult.

235
00:15:53,519 --> 00:15:54,453
Yes.

236
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:56,722
Prioritizing lifespan extension,

237
00:15:57,423 --> 00:16:01,193
I would like to use
FOLFOX 6 and Cetuximab.

238
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:04,763
Then I'd like to operate after that.

239
00:16:05,597 --> 00:16:08,901
If we sit around like Dr. Ebina,

240
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:12,137
Dr. Hiruma will die,

241
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:14,773
let alone get surgery.

242
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:17,676
It would be best to try
a single stage extended operation.

243
00:16:17,743 --> 00:16:21,680
Remove the transverse colon
cancer with the porta hepatis.

244
00:16:21,747 --> 00:16:25,985
Also, a radical operation
for the colon cancer.

245
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:29,855
May I?

246
00:16:29,922 --> 00:16:32,024
Please do.

247
00:16:39,064 --> 00:16:41,734
The porta hepatis's lesion

248
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:45,971
could've infiltrated
the inferior vena cava.

249
00:16:46,038 --> 00:16:47,606
Dr. Ebina's idea

250
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:52,444
will take too long for tumor
reduction with anti-cancer drugs.

251
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:55,314
And inferior vena caval occlusion too.

252
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:57,883
- Well, yes...
- Yes.

253
00:16:57,950 --> 00:17:01,453
With Dr. Kaji's idea, isn't there a need

254
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:05,724
to be a little more careful
with the method?

255
00:17:05,791 --> 00:17:07,359
Yes, that's right.

256
00:17:07,926 --> 00:17:09,828
You're exactly right, Mr. Tendo.

257
00:17:09,895 --> 00:17:13,699
My doctor name, Shigekatsu Hiruma...

258
00:17:13,766 --> 00:17:16,869
The characters mean
"To prevail against illness."

259
00:17:16,935 --> 00:17:19,271
Understand?

260
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:24,810
I want to fight this illness.

261
00:17:24,877 --> 00:17:27,279
What would you like to do?

262
00:17:27,346 --> 00:17:29,214
Yes. The freelancer...

263
00:17:30,749 --> 00:17:35,087
Would you call Dr. Michiko Daimon?

264
00:17:35,154 --> 00:17:36,355
Mr. Tendo.

265
00:17:36,855 --> 00:17:39,124
Dr. Daimon is currently in surgery.

266
00:17:39,191 --> 00:17:40,759
- What?
- She's operating...

267
00:17:40,826 --> 00:17:44,129
Then get the manager with the melons.

268
00:17:44,196 --> 00:17:45,764
The guy who always wears a smile.

269
00:17:45,831 --> 00:17:48,634
I'm sorry, we can't contact him.

270
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:49,902
Then let me!

271
00:17:49,968 --> 00:17:50,936
No, we will!

272
00:17:51,003 --> 00:17:52,071
Let us do it.

273
00:17:52,137 --> 00:17:53,305
We'll do it.

274
00:17:53,372 --> 00:17:54,373
Enough.

275
00:17:55,474 --> 00:17:56,742
I take back what I said.

276
00:17:57,142 --> 00:17:59,111
I have no hopes for you all.

277
00:18:00,045 --> 00:18:01,313
Thank you.

278
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:11,590
I'll ask again...

279
00:18:12,624 --> 00:18:13,725
So you're a doctor?

280
00:18:24,837 --> 00:18:26,905
Mr. Tendo has worked hard

281
00:18:26,972 --> 00:18:30,609
to realize his dream,
the Japan Healthcare Organization.

282
00:18:30,676 --> 00:18:34,413
It was a treacherous road
with many enemies.

283
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:38,350
Many ministries were against him.

284
00:18:38,417 --> 00:18:42,588
His final enemy was
Ms. Tokachi who disagreed with his plans.

285
00:18:43,021 --> 00:18:44,323
His plans?

286
00:18:45,691 --> 00:18:46,692
Oh, Tendo.

287
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:52,664
He saved the wicked Tokachi
and won her approval.

288
00:18:52,731 --> 00:18:53,999
And was finally able to

289
00:18:54,066 --> 00:18:56,635
take the first step towards

290
00:18:56,702 --> 00:18:59,404
his dreams of healthcare reform.

291
00:18:59,471 --> 00:19:00,906
I'm sorry.

292
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,208
Ron.

293
00:19:04,710 --> 00:19:06,612
Ready?

294
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:08,013
Ron.

295
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:12,417
16,000 points?

296
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:13,685
Yes, sorry.

297
00:19:13,752 --> 00:19:15,888
You're unusually strong today.

298
00:19:16,955 --> 00:19:19,491
You can win if Akira's not here.

299
00:19:19,558 --> 00:19:20,659
You're right.

300
00:19:21,093 --> 00:19:24,596
I guess Akira was bad luck for me.

301
00:19:24,663 --> 00:19:28,500
But where did he go?

302
00:19:29,568 --> 00:19:32,237
He was in Abashiri City last.

303
00:19:32,304 --> 00:19:33,539
Abashiri?

304
00:19:33,605 --> 00:19:35,040
Okinawa when I called.

305
00:19:35,107 --> 00:19:36,375
What?

306
00:19:36,441 --> 00:19:38,844
I wonder if he's really working.

307
00:19:38,911 --> 00:19:41,446
He's warping from north to south too much.

308
00:19:41,513 --> 00:19:44,950
It's weird that he just left too.

309
00:19:48,453 --> 00:19:51,623
Daimon. Worried about Akira?

310
00:19:52,724 --> 00:19:54,126
Of course.

311
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:56,428
He's your only teacher.

312
00:19:56,495 --> 00:19:58,096
Are you kidding?

313
00:19:58,163 --> 00:20:01,400
He was taking my surgery fees.

314
00:20:01,767 --> 00:20:07,172
I'm worried about the money
he pocketed and not Akira.

315
00:20:07,239 --> 00:20:09,975
200 million yen!

316
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:12,211
What if he runs off with it?

317
00:20:12,277 --> 00:20:15,180
That's why I text him every day,

318
00:20:15,814 --> 00:20:17,616
but no answer.

319
00:20:20,485 --> 00:20:22,621
Is something wrong?

320
00:20:22,688 --> 00:20:25,390
Nothing.

321
00:20:25,924 --> 00:20:28,660
Ron. That's 64,000 points.

322
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:32,097
Wait...That's...A double limit?

323
00:20:32,164 --> 00:20:33,699
Michiko's finished.

324
00:20:34,199 --> 00:20:38,303
Is this lady bad luck for me?

325
00:20:39,338 --> 00:20:41,139
- Devil in white.
- I'm an angel.

326
00:20:43,375 --> 00:20:44,810
Good job.

327
00:20:46,578 --> 00:20:48,180
Thank you.

328
00:20:55,821 --> 00:20:58,290
I DIDN'T FAIL

329
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:05,998
This feels so good.

330
00:21:10,202 --> 00:21:11,937
I feel dizzy.

331
00:21:12,838 --> 00:21:16,241
Akira, I'm going out.

332
00:21:22,881 --> 00:21:24,349
Not here.

333
00:21:37,596 --> 00:21:41,099
Akira. Let me borrow 10 yen.

334
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:55,047
Akira.

335
00:21:56,915 --> 00:21:58,317
Eat up.

336
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:03,088
Surgery tomorrow.

337
00:22:03,155 --> 00:22:04,256
Eat up.

338
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:07,459
Yes. Thank you meow.

339
00:22:07,859 --> 00:22:10,062
It's delicious meow.

340
00:22:25,877 --> 00:22:28,480
TABLE TENNIS COURT

341
00:23:02,047 --> 00:23:02,981
Akira?

342
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:05,917
Kin from the cake shop.

343
00:23:05,984 --> 00:23:07,486
I'm a doctor.

344
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:08,720
And I'm not Kin.

345
00:23:08,787 --> 00:23:11,623
I looked for you for an hour.

346
00:23:11,690 --> 00:23:14,993
Dr. Jonouchi said you're at public baths,
clubs, or here.

347
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:16,561
You sure have a lot of hobbies.

348
00:23:16,628 --> 00:23:18,997
- You are?
- Hara Mamoru.

349
00:23:19,831 --> 00:23:23,001
You never have to remember my name.

350
00:23:23,769 --> 00:23:25,103
Come to the hospital.

351
00:23:25,170 --> 00:23:28,173
I won't work on days off.

352
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:30,375
You will. You must.

353
00:23:30,442 --> 00:23:33,612
The patient says it has to be you.

354
00:23:33,678 --> 00:23:34,746
Don't let go.

355
00:23:34,813 --> 00:23:35,714
Not all your power.

356
00:23:35,781 --> 00:23:36,948
That's good.

357
00:23:37,015 --> 00:23:38,884
The patient wants you.

358
00:23:41,553 --> 00:23:42,788
We'll change to

359
00:23:42,854 --> 00:23:45,524
FOLFOXIRI and bevacizumab

360
00:23:45,590 --> 00:23:47,959
to further reduce the tumor size.

361
00:23:48,026 --> 00:23:52,397
This sure is the National
Advanced Medical Care Center.

362
00:23:53,365 --> 00:23:54,699
Not good.

363
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:55,634
What is?

364
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:57,135
What is it?

365
00:23:57,636 --> 00:23:59,571
It's spread to the caudate lobe.

366
00:24:10,449 --> 00:24:13,485
The freelance doctor, Dr. Daimon,

367
00:24:15,220 --> 00:24:17,656
says it's spread to the caudate lobe.

368
00:24:18,056 --> 00:24:23,161
You guys couldn't see that
it spread to the caudate lobe?

369
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:28,200
You couldn't see that... Ouch, ouch.

370
00:24:28,266 --> 00:24:29,634
- Are you okay?
- It hurts.

371
00:24:29,701 --> 00:24:34,339
It's the worst when
cocky doctors like this get cancer.

372
00:24:34,406 --> 00:24:35,674
What?

373
00:24:35,740 --> 00:24:37,175
Even if you scream,

374
00:24:37,242 --> 00:24:41,780
the cancer won't listen
like your subordinates.

375
00:24:45,116 --> 00:24:46,418
Dr. Daimon.

376
00:24:47,385 --> 00:24:49,020
If you do it,

377
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:55,494
this cancer of mine...You can remove it?

378
00:24:55,560 --> 00:24:56,695
I won't do that.

379
00:24:56,761 --> 00:24:57,729
Dr. Daimon!

380
00:24:58,897 --> 00:25:01,733
You have all these juniors you trained.

381
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:02,667
You guys can do it.

382
00:25:05,704 --> 00:25:08,039
No answer?

383
00:25:08,106 --> 00:25:09,274
No answer?

384
00:25:11,443 --> 00:25:12,344
I'm sorry...

385
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:17,415
Could...

386
00:25:17,482 --> 00:25:19,284
she and I be alone?

387
00:25:19,351 --> 00:25:20,285
Yes, sir.

388
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:23,154
That was quick.

389
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:27,325
It's spread to a terrible spot.

390
00:25:28,326 --> 00:25:30,362
You're right,

391
00:25:30,428 --> 00:25:31,796
surgery is too risky.

392
00:25:31,863 --> 00:25:34,900
We cannot let
a great senior die from surgery.

393
00:25:35,300 --> 00:25:36,167
Right?

394
00:25:39,938 --> 00:25:42,774
As my name points out,

395
00:25:43,475 --> 00:25:45,877
I'm the youngest of eleven siblings.

396
00:25:45,944 --> 00:25:48,346
We were very poor,

397
00:25:48,413 --> 00:25:50,181
so we couldn't see a doctor

398
00:25:51,449 --> 00:25:54,119
or buy medicine.

399
00:25:54,886 --> 00:25:59,090
So I studied as hard as I could.

400
00:26:00,825 --> 00:26:05,163
At 15 years old,
I decided that I'd become a doctor.

401
00:26:05,664 --> 00:26:08,233
I got into med school on a scholarship.

402
00:26:09,668 --> 00:26:11,136
Why a doctor?

403
00:26:13,004 --> 00:26:14,606
Why, you ask?

404
00:26:16,308 --> 00:26:19,778
Daimon, why did you become a doctor?

405
00:26:22,013 --> 00:26:27,586
I thought I became
a doctor with a noble ambition.

406
00:26:29,621 --> 00:26:30,488
However...

407
00:26:32,290 --> 00:26:35,327
Once I entered
an organization called a hospital,

408
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:40,432
I was filled with the desire
to rise to the top.

409
00:26:42,233 --> 00:26:47,339
As a result, I deceived people
and made lots of enemies.

410
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:53,244
I did many terrible things to Ebina

411
00:26:53,979 --> 00:26:55,614
back in the day.

412
00:26:56,648 --> 00:27:00,385
It's probably my punishment
that I got this illness.

413
00:27:00,952 --> 00:27:04,656
"Juichiro, you've gone too far."

414
00:27:06,257 --> 00:27:09,427
"Become a good doctor."

415
00:27:10,895 --> 00:27:15,166
I feel like god is saying that to me.

416
00:27:18,169 --> 00:27:20,071
Dr. Daimon...

417
00:27:20,939 --> 00:27:22,407
Dr. Daimon...

418
00:27:22,474 --> 00:27:24,175
- Oh...
- Hey!

419
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:26,378
It's not that sad.

420
00:27:26,444 --> 00:27:32,083
If I can have you operate on me...

421
00:27:33,551 --> 00:27:36,488
And my life is spared...

422
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:42,961
I'll work only to
save the lives of patients.

423
00:27:43,361 --> 00:27:45,430
That's how I'll spend my life.

424
00:27:47,365 --> 00:27:49,668
Please. I'm begging you.

425
00:27:50,635 --> 00:27:52,570
Operate on me.

426
00:27:55,907 --> 00:27:57,042
Daimon.

427
00:27:58,576 --> 00:28:00,478
Dr. Hiruma is going this far,

428
00:28:01,179 --> 00:28:02,480
so say yes.

429
00:28:02,547 --> 00:28:04,783
Ebina.

430
00:28:04,849 --> 00:28:06,418
Not now.

431
00:28:06,818 --> 00:28:08,053
I must.

432
00:28:09,487 --> 00:28:10,855
Daimon, please.

433
00:28:12,123 --> 00:28:13,324
Please.

434
00:28:15,894 --> 00:28:16,928
Daimon...

435
00:28:18,596 --> 00:28:20,465
- Yes?
- I won't do that.

436
00:28:22,734 --> 00:28:25,236
I said you guys can do it.

437
00:28:28,740 --> 00:28:32,977
Then we will operate on you.

438
00:28:33,044 --> 00:28:34,045
No.

439
00:28:34,112 --> 00:28:36,715
I swear to god we won't fail.

440
00:28:40,719 --> 00:28:41,686
Ebina.

441
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:46,257
You promise?

442
00:28:46,324 --> 00:28:47,892
Yes, sir. I do.

443
00:28:49,928 --> 00:28:50,795
You promise?

444
00:28:50,862 --> 00:28:52,263
Yes, sir.

445
00:28:52,330 --> 00:28:54,566
Ouch...

446
00:28:54,966 --> 00:28:56,267
I'm here on my day off

447
00:28:56,334 --> 00:28:58,703
because my manager's not here.

448
00:28:59,237 --> 00:29:04,442
Hurry up and come home already.

449
00:29:09,881 --> 00:29:12,317
Akira?

450
00:29:14,052 --> 00:29:16,955
Wait. Hold on.

451
00:29:43,114 --> 00:29:44,816
Sorry. Ron.

452
00:29:46,918 --> 00:29:48,386
8,000 points.

453
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:49,454
Akira!

454
00:29:50,155 --> 00:29:51,790
Oh no. It's Michiko.

455
00:29:51,856 --> 00:29:54,259
What are you doing here?

456
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:56,861
Can't you see?

457
00:29:56,928 --> 00:29:57,829
Mahjong.

458
00:29:59,964 --> 00:30:03,535
DR. TENDO

459
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:07,772
Getting business was a lie.

460
00:30:10,508 --> 00:30:11,743
That's terrible.

461
00:30:12,410 --> 00:30:14,312
You got hospitalized without telling.

462
00:30:18,850 --> 00:30:19,984
What's wrong?

463
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:24,689
Here and here.

464
00:30:26,357 --> 00:30:27,192
I'll do it.

465
00:30:27,258 --> 00:30:28,193
No.

466
00:30:28,259 --> 00:30:29,727
Why?

467
00:30:30,361 --> 00:30:33,798
Dr. Daimon charges a huge surgery fee.

468
00:30:34,699 --> 00:30:38,436
But it's because I,
the manager, kept raising prices.

469
00:30:40,405 --> 00:30:44,475
I'll have a cheaper doctor
with free time do it.

470
00:30:44,542 --> 00:30:45,810
Don't worry.

471
00:30:46,578 --> 00:30:48,213
Some crummy doctor?

472
00:30:48,279 --> 00:30:50,949
It's fine. It's not serious.

473
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:53,918
You do surgery with a bigger fee

474
00:30:53,985 --> 00:30:55,420
and earn lots.

475
00:30:56,187 --> 00:30:57,055
Right.

476
00:30:57,121 --> 00:30:59,257
Sorry, let's continue.

477
00:31:00,291 --> 00:31:01,326
Alright.

478
00:31:02,527 --> 00:31:06,564
I'll win a big hand again.

479
00:31:10,001 --> 00:31:11,769
Yes, Dr. Daimon?

480
00:31:11,836 --> 00:31:13,204
Show me Akira's charts.

481
00:31:14,505 --> 00:31:16,641
Why didn't you tell me?

482
00:31:18,343 --> 00:31:20,678
Show me his charts.

483
00:31:21,613 --> 00:31:22,547
I'll get her out.

484
00:31:24,148 --> 00:31:26,417
Stop. Let go.

485
00:31:27,252 --> 00:31:28,753
Let her see them.

486
00:31:38,096 --> 00:31:38,930
No...

487
00:31:43,701 --> 00:31:46,971
Are these really Akira's?

488
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:53,845
As per his request, we did not notify you.

489
00:31:56,781 --> 00:31:59,817
His lung cancer has infiltrated the aorta.

490
00:32:00,618 --> 00:32:04,622
Of all places, it's the aortic arch.

491
00:32:05,390 --> 00:32:08,993
Brain metastasis
to the right frontal lobe,

492
00:32:09,694 --> 00:32:11,663
and complications of angina too.

493
00:32:16,634 --> 00:32:17,902
I'm sure you know...

494
00:32:19,103 --> 00:32:21,105
But it is inoperable.

495
00:32:27,845 --> 00:32:29,647
And you're a doctor?

496
00:32:32,283 --> 00:32:33,651
You're his physician,

497
00:32:34,352 --> 00:32:37,555
and you're giving up
without doing anything?

498
00:32:39,557 --> 00:32:42,060
He does not wish for surgery.

499
00:32:51,836 --> 00:32:53,905
It means there are operations

500
00:32:55,373 --> 00:32:58,209
that even you cannot do.

501
00:33:19,197 --> 00:33:20,031
Dr. Daimon.

502
00:33:23,134 --> 00:33:24,369
So you knew too.

503
00:33:25,937 --> 00:33:30,308
I'm sorry. Mr. Tendo told me not to tell.

504
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:35,613
She'd get my clothes
when she went for mahjong.

505
00:33:36,681 --> 00:33:38,316
- Thank you.
- Sure.

506
00:33:40,418 --> 00:33:41,419
Akira.

507
00:33:42,820 --> 00:33:44,222
I'll operate.

508
00:33:44,989 --> 00:33:46,124
Michiko.

509
00:33:47,992 --> 00:33:49,327
Don't be ridiculous.

510
00:33:50,094 --> 00:33:52,930
Surgery will just get me another 3 months.

511
00:33:52,997 --> 00:33:55,466
I can do it, so let me.

512
00:33:55,533 --> 00:33:56,667
No.

513
00:33:57,769 --> 00:33:59,771
No one can operate.

514
00:34:00,338 --> 00:34:01,706
It's too late.

515
00:34:04,809 --> 00:34:09,213
It's fate. Destiny.

516
00:34:10,948 --> 00:34:12,583
- Give it up.
- No.

517
00:34:13,418 --> 00:34:14,385
I won't give up.

518
00:34:21,225 --> 00:34:22,360
Oh yeah.

519
00:34:24,896 --> 00:34:26,764
About the money I pocketed.

520
00:34:27,565 --> 00:34:31,436
I decided to enter
a great hospice with that money.

521
00:34:32,737 --> 00:34:34,672
Mr. Tendo made arrangements,

522
00:34:35,339 --> 00:34:38,209
and I'm waiting for my turn.

523
00:34:38,910 --> 00:34:43,047
Ben Casey will inherit what I have left,

524
00:34:43,114 --> 00:34:44,015
but don't get mad.

525
00:34:44,081 --> 00:34:45,783
I don't care about that.

526
00:34:46,250 --> 00:34:47,885
Akira...

527
00:34:48,486 --> 00:34:50,488
My physician is Mr. Tendo.

528
00:34:53,224 --> 00:34:58,162
Besides, out of all the doctors I've met,

529
00:34:59,163 --> 00:35:00,798
Mr. Tendo understands you the most.

530
00:35:02,333 --> 00:35:06,938
He said that he'd
like to continue to support you.

531
00:35:08,606 --> 00:35:11,476
I asked him to take good care of you.

532
00:35:16,180 --> 00:35:20,518
So it's over between us?

533
00:35:30,561 --> 00:35:31,596
That's right.

534
00:35:35,099 --> 00:35:39,937
I'll...Go to a luxurious hospice

535
00:35:41,305 --> 00:35:42,807
and die a luxurious death.

536
00:35:45,042 --> 00:35:47,378
Don't come see me anymore.

537
00:35:57,188 --> 00:35:58,556
Fine.

538
00:35:59,957 --> 00:36:01,325
Have your way.

539
00:36:30,655 --> 00:36:32,256
You have a fever.

540
00:36:32,790 --> 00:36:35,059
Any other problems?

541
00:36:36,460 --> 00:36:37,662
A bit right here.

542
00:36:41,499 --> 00:36:45,770
I hear that Dr. Daimon
is an old student of yours.

543
00:36:46,437 --> 00:36:47,305
Yes.

544
00:36:48,773 --> 00:36:50,074
15 years ago...

545
00:36:51,309 --> 00:36:54,111
She came to me in Cuba,

546
00:36:55,313 --> 00:36:57,782
since I knew her late father well.

547
00:36:58,449 --> 00:37:00,318
To be my assistant.

548
00:37:00,918 --> 00:37:02,820
Was she always that skilled?

549
00:37:03,988 --> 00:37:05,122
Not at all.

550
00:37:07,024 --> 00:37:11,862
Like her father,
she had a great gift for surgery.

551
00:37:13,931 --> 00:37:17,201
But she was so clumsy and timid.

552
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:21,973
I'm amazed she hung in there.

553
00:37:29,347 --> 00:37:32,617
EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT

554
00:37:41,192 --> 00:37:42,627
Cut in one stroke.

555
00:37:44,895 --> 00:37:45,963
One stroke!

556
